  "answer_text": "Great question! \"Funnest\" is pretty subjective in Terraria, but here's a breakdown of all four classes and what makes each one enjoyable:\n\n---\n\nThere are **four official Terraria classes: Mage, Summoner, Melee, and Ranged.** Here's what the community generally thinks about each:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddd9 **Mage** \u2014 Most Popular Pick\nIn general, the **Mage class is one of the most popular.** Each attack feels fairly unique, so you bring multiple weapons for multiple situations. The huge variety of spells keeps gameplay fresh throughout the entire run. The downside is it can be tough early on due to low defense.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udc80 **Summoner** \u2014 Most Unique Playstyle\nMany players argue that **Summoner** is the most fun to play \u2014 the feeling of having an army of minions fighting for you is great. It's a rather hard class but fun to play, and the **Terraprisma** is what makes Summoner most worthwhile in the endgame.\n\n---\n\n### \u2694\ufe0f **Melee** \u2014 Most Satisfying\nThe **Melee class** is Terraria's version of the Warrior archetype commonly found in most RPGs \u2014 they're the close-ranged damage dealers that always stay close to enemy lines. With Melee, you get cool anime-style swords with projectiles, and of course the legendary **Zenith** sword at endgame is one of the most satisfying weapons in the game.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udff9 **Ranger** \u2014 Most Consistent\n**Rangers** are a very powerful class that focuses on doing massive damage while keeping away from their foes. Many consider Ranger to be the best class overall \u2014 it has a good amount of defense and is the most consistent class in the game. However, some find it a bit less visually exciting than the others.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc6 **So, which is the FUNNEST?**\nIt really comes down to your playstyle:\n- \ud83e\uddd9 **Mage** \u2014 if you love variety and flashy spells\n- \ud83d\udc80 **Summoner** \u2014 if you love a unique, strategic \"army\" playstyle\n- \u2694\ufe0f **Melee** \u2014 if you love being in the action with big, satisfying weapons\n- \ud83c\udff9 **Ranger** \u2014 if you love power and consistency without much risk\n\nFor a **first playthrough**, most players recommend **Mage** or **Melee** for the most fun experience!",
